摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Hash-anchored read/edit/grep tools for DeepSeek Harness: every line carries a content hash, stale anchors are rejected before touching the file.","id":"gh:1333756247","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-tool-hashline","slug":"InklingYoshi584/dsh-tool-hashline","topics":["dsh-plugin","hashline"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Hash-anchored read/edit/grep tools for DeepSeek Harness: every line carries a content hash, stale an"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"chors are rejected before touching the file."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-tool-hashline"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Hash-anchored `read`, `edit`, and `grep` tools for DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Every line carries a shor"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"t content hash; edits reference `LINE#HASH` anchors that are verified against the file's current con"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"tent **before anything is written**. Stale anchors fail the whole call — never relocated, never fuzz"},{"id":"p3s4","text":"y-matched, never silently applied to the wrong line."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Protocol adopted from pi-hashline-edit (MIT), inspired by oh-my-pi."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## How to install"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"### Prerequisites"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **Node.js ≥ 20** (for running dsh and the plugin).\n- **dsh**. Two ways to have it:\n- No install: `"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"npx @deepseek-ai/dsh <command>` — note the bare command always needs a profile: `npx @deepseek-ai/ds"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"h web` or `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh --profile headless \"task\"`.\n- Global install (gives you the bare `ds"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"h` command on PATH, plus pnpm in one go): `npm i -g pnpm @deepseek-ai/dsh`.\n- **pnpm** — the `dsh pl"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"ugin` command forwards to it (installed by the global command above).\n- A **DeepSeek API key** for l"},{"id":"p7s6","text":"ive sessions (configure it in the Web UI at Settings → Models, or export `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`)."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"### Step 1 — get the plugin"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"**Option A: npm (recommended)** — published on the registry, installs the prebuilt `lib/` bundle:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"**Option B: from source** (development):"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"The `@deepseek-ai/*` harness packages are dev dependencies here on purpose: at runtime the plugin re"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"solves them from the dsh installation through the profile's maintained flat fallback (`$DSH_HOME/pro"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"files/node_modules` symlinks), so no duplicate harness core ever ships with the plugin. `npm install"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"` only needs to succeed for the tests; running the plugin needs nothing but the preset row."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"### Step 2 — author the `hashline` preset"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"The plugin replaces the stock tools by **preset-plane shadowing**: a preset that mounts this plugin "},{"id":"p15s2","text":"instead of `tool-fs` gives its sessions the hashline `read`/`edit`/`grep` while everything else keep"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"s working from the host composition. Create the preset by dropping the shipped files into the user p"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"reset root (hand-created presets are discovered live):"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"…or use the Web UI (Settings → presets → copy `standard` as `hashline`) and replace the copied compo"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"sition with the shipped template."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Then edit the plugin row in `$DSH_HOME/.agent-presets/hashline/agent.cordis.yml` to point at your in"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"dit the plugin row in `$DSH_HOME/.agent-presets/hashline/agent.cordis.yml` to point at your install:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"To also enable grep, add `config: { grep: true }` to that row."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"### Step 3 — select the preset"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Settings → presets → `hashline`, or set the default in `$DSH_HOME/settings.yaml`:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"New sessions now run on hashline. Sessions already running keep their composition — only new session"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"s pick up the preset."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"### Step 4 — verify it works"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"1. In a session: **read any text file** — output lines are `LINE#HASH:` tagged (`   1#PK:alpha`).\n2."},{"id":"p26s2","text":" Ask the agent to **edit something** — the call carries `edits: [{op, pos: \"N#HASH\", …}]` and the re"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"sult returns an `--- Anchors ---` block.\n3. Settings → Agent presets should show **\"In use: Hashline"},{"id":"p26s4","text":" returns an `--- Anchors ---` block.\n3. Settings → Agent presets should show **\"In use: Hashline\"**."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"### What the swap changes"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"On the `hashline` preset, `read`/`edit` (and `grep` when enabled) are the hashline versions — the pr"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"eset's scope layer shadows the global `tool-fs`/`tool-fs-search` tools **by name**. `write`, `read_i"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"mage`, `glob`, `bash`, and everything else keep working from the host composition, and subagents inh"},{"id":"p28s4","text":"bash`, and everything else keep working from the host composition, and subagents inherit the preset."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"### Headless / no-roster deployments"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"The `headless` profile composes no preset roster. Use a `--patch` overlay with a host-plane swap ins"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"headless` profile composes no preset roster. Use a `--patch` overlay with a host-plane swap instead:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Why use it"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"AI coding agents edit files by quoting what they saw on screen. Two things can be true at edit time:"},{"id":"p34s2","text":" the file changed since the read (a concurrent write, a drift, an earlier edit in the same turn), an"},{"id":"p34s3","text":"d the quoted text appears in more than one place. Stock edit tools handle this badly:"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"- **Literal string-replace** (`old_string`/`new_string`, what DSH ships) requires the quoted text to"},{"id":"p35s2","text":" match *exactly once*. Any drift means a retry loop; ambiguity means \"make it more specific\" busywor"},{"id":"p35s3","text":"k.\n- **Line-number editing** is worse: numbers silently point at the *wrong* line after any shift, a"},{"id":"p35s4","text":"nd the edit corrupts code the model never looked at.\n- The problem is real enough that Cursor traine"},{"id":"p35s5","text":"d a dedicated 70B model just to apply edits correctly."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"The evidence that the harness — not the model — is the lever: Can Balioglu's benchmark kept 15 model"},{"id":"p36s2","text":"s fixed and swapped only the edit format. Hashline beat patch for 14 of 16 configurations, **and the"},{"id":"p36s3","text":" weakest models gained the most**. Better anchoring rescues the long tail of models you'd otherwise "},{"id":"p36s4","text":"dels gained the most**. Better anchoring rescues the long tail of models you'd otherwise give up on."},{"id":"p37s1","text":"What hashline changes:"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"| Property | Stock `edit` | hashline |"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"| Anchor | literal `old_string` text | `LINE#HASH` content hash |\n| File drifted since read | error,"},{"id":"p39s2","text":" retry with new text | error **naming the stale anchor**, re-read, retry |\n| Same line text appears "},{"id":"p39s3","text":"twice | ambiguity, \"be more specific\" | context hashing makes collisions rare; ambiguity lists candi"},{"id":"p39s4","text":"dates |\n| Multiple hunks | one call per hunk | **N ops in one call**, one snapshot, one atomic write"},{"id":"p39s5","text":" |\n| After an edit | re-read the file | fresh `--- Anchors ---` block → chained edits with no re-rea"},{"id":"p39s6","text":"d |\n| Search-to-edit | grep, then open, then quote | `grep` returns the same anchors → edit with no "},{"id":"p39s7","text":"to-edit | grep, then open, then quote | `grep` returns the same anchors → edit with no read at all |"},{"id":"p40s1","text":"On top of that, DSH's own observation policy stays in force: read-before-write and a file-level vers"},{"id":"p40s2","text":"ion CAS still guard the whole file, while the anchors guard the *lines*. You get line-level correctn"},{"id":"p40s3","text":"ess and file-level freshness together."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
